msgid "Krita Monthly Update – Edition 16"
msgstr "Krita Monata Ĝisdatigo - Eldono 16"

#: content/en/posts/2024/monthly-update-16.md:9
msgid "Krita is 25 years old!"
msgstr "Krita havas 25 jarojn!"

#: content/en/posts/2024/monthly-update-16.md:11
msgid ""
"![krita_25th_davidrevoy_ccbysa](images/posts/2024/david-kiki-krita-25.jpeg) "
"*Artwork by [David Revoy](https://www.davidrevoy.com/article1031/happy-25th-"
"anniversary-krita) (CC BY-SA)*"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/monthly-update-16.md:14
msgid ""
"May 31, 2024 marks Krita’s 25th birthday. As one would expect, there have "
"been many changes over the years – even the name changed several times. You "
"can get a look inside Krita’s history in this [blog post written by @Halla]"
"(https://krita.org/en/posts/2024/krita-25-years/), Krita’s Maintainer for "
"more than 20 years."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/monthly-update-16.md:16
msgid ""
"In honour of this milestone, @RamonM prepared a special treat for all Krita "
"users: a video interview with @Halla."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/monthly-update-16.md:20
msgid "Your feedback is requested"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/monthly-update-16.md:22
msgid ""
"5.2.3-Beta1 was released June 5th. This release represents a complete rework "
"of the build system and numerous fixes by the core Krita developer team as "
"well as [freyalupen](https://krita-artists.org/u/freyalupen), [Grum999]"
"(https://krita-artists.org/u/grum999), [NabilMaghfurUsman](https://krita-"
"artists.org/u/nabilmaghfurusman), [Deif_Lou](https://krita-artists.org/u/"
"deif_lou), Alvin Wong, Rasyuqa A. H. and Mathias Wein. There are a number of "
"first-time contributors whose names appear next to their contribution in the "
"[release notes](https://krita.org/en/posts/2024/krita-5-2-3-beta1/)."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/monthly-update-16.md:24
msgid ""
"Testing packages for every platform are provided on the release notes page. "
"Please report your findings and feedback in the [Testers Wanted](https://"
"krita-artists.org/t/testers-wanted-5-2-3-beta1-issues-and-feedback-"
"thread/93122) thread."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/monthly-update-16.md:27
msgid ""
"Text property editing: Merge request [2092](https://invent.kde.org/graphics/"
"krita/-/merge_requests/2092) is almost finished, awaiting review. Testing "
"builds are now available on the CI. @Wolthera is requesting user feedback on "
"the UX. Please read [this post](https://krita-artists.org/t/text-tool-"
"thread/57973/102) and share your comments there."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/monthly-update-16.md:28
msgid ""
"Google Summer of Code (GSOC) @Ken_Lo is seeking input on the Pixel Perfect "
"project https://krita-artists.org/t/pixel-perfect-line-setting-for-pixel-art-"
"brushes/42629/16"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/monthly-update-16.md:30
#: content/en/posts/2024/monthly-update-17.md:34
#: content/en/posts/2024/monthly-update-18.md:24
msgid "Other Development Highlights"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/monthly-update-16.md:32
msgid ""
"[Free transform bounding box rotation](https://invent.kde.org/graphics/"
"krita/-/merge_requests/2113) by [Stuffin](https://krita-artists.org/u/"
"stuffin) has been merged. This completes the feature request [Adjusting the "
"transform box to match the object angle in the drawing](https://krita-"
"artists.org/t/adjusting-the-transform-box-to-match-the-object-angle-in-the-"
"drawing/63687) and can be tested in the 5.3.0-prealpha nightly. (Note to "
"testers: Adjusting the bounding box is activated with Ctrl+Alt.) Thanks "
"stuffin!"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/monthly-update-16.md:37
msgid ""
"Grum999 is improving the python API so that it is more robust for python "
"developers and they can access more of krita’s internal features through "
"python. There is a work-in-progress MR to add new scripting functions for "
"accessing Grids, Guides, and Mirror Axes from the document, and signals for "
"changes in the document and view. [Check the MR](https://invent.kde.org/"
"graphics/krita/-/merge_requests/2147)"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/monthly-update-16.md:39
msgid ""
"@Ralek has added lossless transformation conditions - Rotations in "
"increments of 90 degrees, and perfect x and y mirrors should now be "
"lossless. This should greatly help out pixel artists, who I believe "
"previously could not use these functions at all. [Check the MR](https://"
"invent.kde.org/graphics/krita/-/merge_requests/2137)"
msgstr ""

