"Welcome to the [@Krita-promo](https://krita-artists.org/groups/krita-promo) "
"team's October 2024 development and community update."
msgstr ""
"Bonvenon al la disvolviĝa kaj komunuma ĝisdatigo de la teamo [@Krita-promo]"
"(https://krita-artists.org/groups/krita-promo) por Oktobro 2024."

#: content/en/posts/2024/monthly-update-20.md:8
msgid "Android-only Krita 5.2.8 Hotfix Release"
msgstr "Nur-Androida Flikaĵa Eldono 5.2.8 de Krita"

#: content/en/posts/2024/monthly-update-20.md:9
msgid ""
"Krita 5.2.6 was reported to crash on startup on devices running Android 14 "
"or later. This was caused by issues with an SDK update required for release "
"on the Play Store, so a temporary 5.2.7 release reverting it was available "
"from the downloads page only."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/monthly-update-20.md:11
msgid ""
"However, the issue has now been resolved and 5.2.8 is rolling out on the "
"Play Store. Note that 5.2.8 raises the minimum supported Android version to "
"Android 7.0 (Nougat)."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/monthly-update-20.md:13
msgid "Community Bug Hunt Started"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/monthly-update-20.md:14
msgid ""
"The development team has declared a \"Bug Hunt Month\" running through "
"November, and needs the community's help to decide what to do with each and "
"every one of the hundreds of open bug reports on the bug tracker. Which "
"reports are valid and need to be fixed? Which ones need more info or are "
"already resolved?"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2024/monthly-update-20.md:16
msgid ""
"Read the bug hunting guide and join in on the [bug hunt thread on the Krita-"
"Artists forum](https://krita-artists.org/t/volunteers-needed-krita-bughunt-"
"month-started/104916)."
msgstr ""

