#: content/en/posts/2026/krita-5.3.0-released.md:0
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "Krita 5.2.1 Released"
msgid "Krita 5.3.0 Released!"
msgstr "Krita 5.2.1 Eldonita"

#: content/en/posts/2026/krita-5.3.0-released.md:8
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "First Beta for Krita 5.2.3 Released"
msgid "Today is the simultaneous release of Krita 5.3.0 and Krita 6.0.0!"
msgstr "Unua Beta por Krita 5.2.3 Eldonita"

#: content/en/posts/2026/krita-5.3.0-released.md:10
msgid ""
"Depending which version of Qt and KDE Frameworks you build, the same source "
"will result in one of the other. Both versions are almost functionally "
"identical, with 6.0.0 having more Wayland functionality."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2026/krita-5.3.0-released.md:12
msgid ""
"But note that since Krita 6 is still considered rather experimental, since "
"it's our first release based on Qt 6, and there were many complicated "
"changes between 5 and 6."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2026/krita-5.3.0-released.md:14
msgid ""
"For real work, please use 5.3.0! We expect 6.0 to become the main version of "
"Krita before the end of the year, though."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2026/krita-5.3.0-released.md:16
msgid "What's New"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2026/krita-5.3.0-released.md:18
msgid ""
"{{< video-player src=\"https://cdn.kde.org/krita/marketing/videos/"
"krita-53-60-trailer.mp4\" thumbnail=\"images/"
"release_notes/2026-03-02_krita-53-60-trailer_thumbnail.jpg\" type=\"video/"
"mp4\" >}} Video courtesy of [David Revoy](https://davidrevoy.com)."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2026/krita-5.3.0-released.md:21
msgid ""
"Krita 5.3/6.0 is the result of many years of work by the Krita developers. "
"Some features have been rewritten from the ground up, others make their "
"first appearance."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2026/krita-5.3.0-released.md:23
msgid ""
"Enjoy the completely new text feature: on canvas editing, full opentype "
"support, text flowing into shapes. It is now easier than ever to create "
"vector-based panels for comic pages. Tools got extended: for instance, the "
"fill tool now can close gaps. The liquify mode of the transform tool is much "
"faster. There are new filters: a propagate colors filter and a reset "
"transparent filter. Support for HDR painting has been improved. The recorder "
"docker can now work in real time. There is improved support for file "
"formats, like support for text objects in PSD files. And much, much, much "
"more!"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2026/krita-5.3.0-released.md:25
msgid ""
"For a complete overview of everything, check out our extensive [release "
"notes](https://krita.org/en/release-notes/krita-5-3-release-notes/)!"
msgstr ""

