#: content/en/posts/2026/krita-5.3.1-released.md:9
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "First Beta for Krita 5.2.3 Released"
msgid "Today we're releasing Krita 5.3.1 and 6.0.1."
msgstr "Unua Beta por Krita 5.2.3 Eldonita"

#: content/en/posts/2026/krita-5.3.1-released.md:11
msgid ""
"This release mainly fixes an issue for Windows users: some applications, "
"like Microsoft Windows Powertoys' Fancy Zones or the Google Drive plugin "
"cause problems for Krita. These applications query all running applications "
"for their accessibility abilities."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2026/krita-5.3.1-released.md:13
msgid ""
"Until [Qt6](https://github.com/qt/qtbase/commit/"
"bcd0a3220348778c0d72faac202efb97f4d6dd07), Qt's QML module, which is used "
"extensively in the new text tool, would then recursively query all active "
"screen objects, like comboboxes or buttons, and up and down the entire class "
"hierarchy for accessibility features. This slowed down Krita to the point "
"where even menus would be slow to open."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2026/krita-5.3.1-released.md:15
msgid ""
"It was extremely tricky to figure this out, since none of the Krita "
"developers actually use these external applications... But it should be "
"fixed now!"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2026/krita-5.3.1-released.md:17
msgid "There are more fixes in this release:"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2026/krita-5.3.1-released.md:19
msgid ""
"The mutator shortcut is now Ctrl-alt-shift-m instead of Z in accordance with "
"the plugin's manual."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2026/krita-5.3.1-released.md:20
msgid "On Android, the canvas will not pan up when you use the text tool"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2026/krita-5.3.1-released.md:21
msgid "On Android, the OnePlus stylus middle click button works"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2026/krita-5.3.1-released.md:22
msgid "Animation Key Frame copy pasting now works in Krita 6"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2026/krita-5.3.1-released.md:23
msgid ""
"On Wayland, drag and drop is fixed (Wayland clears the clipboard when a new "
"window is opened, so now we have to cache the data.)"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2026/krita-5.3.1-released.md:24
msgid ""
"The canvas resize dialog now works correctly when changing units ([bug: "
"517857](https://bugs.kde.org/517857))"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2026/krita-5.3.1-released.md:25
msgid "The Incremental Backup/Version saving function now works in Krita 6."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2026/krita-5.3.1-released.md:26
msgid ""
"On Android, text fields should no longer block stylus movements, pressing "
"spacebar should work as a shortcut and the view should no longer turn blue "
"when pressing a keyboard key. These issues only occurred on some devices."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2026/krita-5.3.1-released.md:28
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "The [release notes](en/release-notes/krita-5-2-release-notes/) will give "
#| "you all the details, but here are some highlights:"
msgid ""
"Check out the [release notes](https://krita.org/en/release-notes/krita-5-3-"
"release-notes/) for a full overview of all the new features in Krita 5.3 and "
"6.0."
msgstr ""
"La [eldonaj notoj](eo/release-notes/krita-5-2-release-notes/) donos al vi "
"ĉiujn detalojn, sed jen kelkaj elstaraĵoj:"

#: content/en/posts/2026/krita-5.3.1-released.md:31
msgid ""
"[!WARNING] One again, we consider Krita 5.3.1 suitable for productive work; "
"6.0.1 is, because of the many changes from Qt5 to Qt6 more experimental."
msgstr ""

