#: content/en/posts/2026/monthly-report-2602.md:12
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "Krita 5.2.1 Released"
msgid "5.2.15 Released"
msgstr "Krita 5.2.1 Eldonita"

#: content/en/posts/2026/monthly-report-2602.md:13
msgid ""
"5.2.15, another bugfix release, is out, featuring a few more Android, touch "
"input, and general bug fixes. This is really the last 5.2.x release this "
"time."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2026/monthly-report-2602.md:15
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "The following fixes were made in response to all your bug reports for the "
#| "[first release candidate](https://krita.org/en/item/krita-5-2-release-"
#| "candidate-is-out/):"
msgid ""
"Check out the [5.2.15 release post](https://krita.org/en/posts/2026/"
"krita-5.2.15-released/) and stay up-to-date!"
msgstr ""
"La sekvaj korektoj estis faritaj en respondo al ĉiuj viaj cimraportoj por la "
"[unua eldona kandidato](https://krita.org/en/item/krita-5-2-release-"
"candidate-is-out/):"

#: content/en/posts/2026/monthly-report-2602.md:17
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "First Beta for Krita 5.2.0 Released"
msgid "First Beta for 5.3.0/6.0.0 Released"
msgstr "Unua Beta por Krita 5.2.0 Eldonita"

#: content/en/posts/2026/monthly-report-2602.md:18
msgid ""
"The next major release will be a dual release; 5.3.0 is built on the "
"familiar Qt5 framework, while 6.0.0 is ported to the newer Qt6 framework. "
"Qt6 allows for better Wayland compositor support on Linux among other "
"things, but unfamiliarity and lack of testing means Krita 6.0.0 will be less "
"stable than 5.3.0. Krita 6 is also not yet available on Android."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2026/monthly-report-2602.md:20
msgid ""
"The first betas for this release are out. Help out by testing the two years' "
"worth of changes since 5.2 and the Qt6 porting work, and [report any bugs "
"you find](https://docs.krita.org/en/untranslatable_pages/reporting_bugs."
"html) so they can be fixed before the final release! Learn more in the "
"[beta1 release post](https://krita.org/en/posts/2026/krita-5.3-6.0-first-"
"beta.md)."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2026/monthly-report-2602.md:22
msgid "Some of Last Month's Bugfixes"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2026/monthly-report-2602.md:23
msgid ""
"The team has been busy polishing new features and fixing old bugs for the "
"beta release."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2026/monthly-report-2602.md:25
msgid ""
"Many issues with gradients, layer styles, and resource loading were fixed by "
"Dmitry."
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2026/monthly-report-2602.md:26
msgid ""
"Layer Styles now use their own copy of gradients, preventing the gradients "
"from unexpectedly changing when the global version is modified, as well as "
"related crashes. ([bug 1]({{<bug-url 505986>}}), [bug 2]({{<bug-url "
"510082>}}), [bug 3]({{<bug-url 467729>}}), [bug 4]({{<bug-url 514744>}}); "
"[change]({{<commit-url 97fbf20faf>}}))"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2026/monthly-report-2602.md:27
msgid ""
"The Bevel-and-Emboss Layer Style now saves patterns correctly. ([bug]({{<bug-"
"url 510082>}}); [change]({{<commit-url 8c854aaea6>}}))"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2026/monthly-report-2602.md:28
msgid ""
"Brush presets with embedded resources sharing a name with a different "
"resource are now loaded correctly. (CC[bug]({{<bug-url 514744>}}); [change]"
"({{<commit-url d86c29e217>}}))"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2026/monthly-report-2602.md:29
msgid ""
"Fixed editing or removing resource bundles causing a database error on "
"startup. ([bug]({{<bug-url 508096>}}); [change]({{<commit-url 34c55c0bb3>}}))"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2026/monthly-report-2602.md:31
msgid "More text fixes by Wolthera:"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2026/monthly-report-2602.md:32
msgid ""
"Made sure new texts are made with the current foreground color. ([change]"
"({{<commit-url 85ea954c4b>}}))"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2026/monthly-report-2602.md:33
msgid ""
"Fixed an issue where light-colored text made Krita stall and then the text "
"disappeared (caused by reading uninitialized data as font metrics). ([bug]"
"({{<bug-url 504814>}}); [change]({{<commit-url 79b6fe0120>}}))"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2026/monthly-report-2602.md:34
msgid ""
"Fixed selecting fonts whose full name is the same as their family name. "
"([bug]({{<bug-url 514300>}}); [change]({{<commit-url 645ed3a967>}}))"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2026/monthly-report-2602.md:35
msgid ""
"Fixed freeze when editing text contour while bound rect snapping is enabled. "
"([change]({{<commit-url f49c72d8be>}}))"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2026/monthly-report-2602.md:36
msgid ""
"Fixed setting subscript and superscript on the entire paragraph. ([bug]"
"({{<bug-url 426607>}}); [change]({{<commit-url 1a1f118c35>}}))"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2026/monthly-report-2602.md:38
msgid ""
"The G'MIC filter plugin has been updated by Ivan to [version 3.6.6](https://"
"discuss.pixls.us/t/release-of-gmic-3-6/47481). ([change]({{<merge-request-"
"url 2603>}}))"
msgstr ""

#: content/en/posts/2026/monthly-report-2602.md:40
msgid ""
"On macOS, Krita's G'MIC is now faster, being built with OpenMP's "
"multithreading as was already the case on other platforms. ([change]"
"({{<merge-request-url 2607>}}))"
msgstr ""

